1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
NEN

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,000
[narrator] Nen abilities fall into
the following six distinct categories:

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Enhancers are able
to strengthen and reinforce

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
the natural properties
of any object they encounter.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Transmuters can manipulate and change
the quality of aura at will.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Similar to Transmuters,

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Conjurers have the ability
to materialize an object out of aura.

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Emitters can propel their aura,

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
shooting or projecting it forward.

10
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Manipulators can use their aura
to control objects or living things.

11
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Specialists possess rare abilities

12
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
which do not fit
within the other five categories.

13
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,000
One must determine
which category their aura falls into.

14
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
This is the first step
to becoming a skilled Nen user.

15
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,000
[theme song playing]

16
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
The auction, as you all know,

17
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,000
will begin in one month.

18
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Before that time,
find one item from the list provided

19
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
and then bring it safely back here.

20
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,000
[surprised gasp]

21
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
THE EYEBALLS OF A KURTA

22
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,000
[breathes heavily]

23
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,000
[man on the screen] If you’re successful,
you’ll be hired

24
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:37,000
and begin your training
in security and acquisitions.

25
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,000
[Kurapika] In all likelihood,

26
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,000
the man we saw was not the actual client,

27
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,000
thus, illustrating the distance
between the client and myself.

28
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
It’s critical that I get
as close to them as possible,

29
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,000
until they eventually let their guard down
and share their secrets.

30
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
I will pass this test.

31
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:01,000
First, I must ingratiate myself
and win their trust.

32
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:06,000
NEN x USERS x UNITE

33
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,000
[man] Hey… It won’t open.

34
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Huh?

35
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
[man on the screen]
I forgot to mention one thing.

36
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:16,000
The minimum requirement
for the position is strength.

37
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Enough strength
to get out of this mansion

38
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
with your lives.

39
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,000
[intense music playing]

40
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,000
DOWSING CHAIN:
THE GUIDING RING FINGER CHAIN

41
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
[gunshots]

42
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,000
[groaning in pain]

43
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,000
[man]
He used a chain to stop the bullets!

44
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Impressive.

45
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
-[clatter]
-[chain rattles]

46
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
[grunting]

47
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
[Kurapika] Three with guns.

48
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Six with swords.

49
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Two more with swords above.

50
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Good job concealing your presence, guys.

51
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
But unfortunately for you,
you’re too weak! [grunts]

52
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:53,000
As a matter of fact,
I don’t even need to use my Nen!

53
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,000
[gasps]

54
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,000
So that’s what’s going on.

55
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
I get it now.

56
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,000
It’s him.

57
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,000
[all gasp]

58
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,000
[gasps]

59
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,000
-Call them off right now.
-[grunts]

60
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
I’ll count to three.

61
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,000
One, two…

62
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Okay, okay!

63
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Whatever you say.

64
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
-[gasps]
-Wait. What’s going on?

65
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:39,000
They were made of Nen.

66
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
I knew as soon as I punched one of ‘em.

67
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:46,000
They’re just masses of aura
shaped like men. They’re weak.

68
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,000
I didn’t realize it was his Nen.

69
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Impressive. How'd you know?

70
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:55,000
You were careful to stand next to
the others for camouflage.

71
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,000
But when I watched you from above,
it was clear.

72
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Every one of us was under attack,
except you.

73
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Oh?

74
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
[Kurapika] I realized something was wrong

75
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,000
when two of them appeared
on the second floor.

76
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,000
After I jumped over to the chandelier
and out of their reach,

77
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
they just stood there,

78
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
continuing to swing their swords,

79
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,000
in a futile attempt to reach me.

80
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,000
I have to assume
they received a basic order

81
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,000
-to attack whichever enemy was nearest.
-[grunts]

82
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,000
The instructions the assailants had
were simple,

83
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
so their attacks were as well.

84
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:35,000
However, it would take
an incredibly skilled Nen user

85
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,000
to control eleven
human-sized aura simultaneously.

86
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,000
And it stands to reason

87
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:44,000
that this Nen user would
most likely be an Emitter.

88
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:47,000
And given the size of the aura involved,

89
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:50,000
he would have to be
within a few meters of the assailants.

90
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,000
Which meant that the Nen user…

91
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
was someone inside this very room.

92
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,000
[whistles]

93
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:01,000
Well, yeah, you nailed it.

94
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,000
My name is Shachmono Tocino.

95
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
As you might’ve guessed, I'm a Hunter.

96
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Of course, I’m also an employee here,

97
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:12,000
which means I’m basically your senior.

98
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:15,000
Now that’s cleared up,
think you could put away your knife?

99
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,000
[sighs]

100
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Based on the chains,

101
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
I think it’s fairly safe to assume
that you’re a Manipulator, aren’t you?

102
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,000
Well, I sure hope you won’t hold a grudge.

103
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:35,000
See, I was only following the orders
the boss gave me.

104
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:38,000
“Test the applicants
by attempting to kill them.”

105
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:42,000
But I honestly never expected
to be exposed so quickly!

106
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Well, I’m willing to bet

107
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:47,000
that the four of you together
should be able to escape the mansion.

108
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,000
So best of luck.

109
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,000
‘Four of you”?

110
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:54,000
That makes it sound like
there’s another one in the room.

111
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,000
[chuckles]

112
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,000
I imagine that was meant to be
some sort of diversion,

113
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,000
but it was the wrong call.

114
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Before we all succumb to paranoia,

115
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:10,000
I shall determine if there are
any other infiltrators among us.

116
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,000
[scoffs]

117
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,000
[grunts]

118
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
[all gasp]

119
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:54,000
There you are.

120
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,000
You are the infiltrator.

121
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,000
[chain rattles]

122
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,000
That’s ridiculous!

123
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,000
What grounds are you basing that on?

124
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
Just ‘cause your chain started swinging?

125
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,000
[short woman] It’s called dowsing.

126
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,000
Huh? And what’s that supposed to mean?

127
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:22,000
[short woman]
Dowsing was originally a technique

128
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:25,000
for locating water or other metals
hidden beneath the ground.

129
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:29,000
But it was also used in divination.

130
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,000
I’ve even heard of the technique

131
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,000
being employed as a kind of lie detector.

132
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,000
Okay, maybe so,

133
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,000
but that still isn’t concrete proof

134
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:40,000
that I’m the infiltrator!
It doesn’t prove anything!

135
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,000
Well, in any case, he’s probably right.

136
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Your heart.

137
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:48,000
I noticed it began to pound
as soon as he pointed his finger at you.

138
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Of course, if you were innocent…

139
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:56,000
your heart rate would have increased
much more gradually

140
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:59,000
due to the stress
of being wrongly accused.

141
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:04,000
But your heartbeat
sped up almost immediately

142
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:07,000
before gradually slowing
back down again.

143
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,000
[light giggle]

144
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:12,000
The typical melody of a liar,
no doubt about it.

145
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,000
-That’s true for both of you.
-Hm?

146
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,000
[cracking knuckles]

147
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,000
Well, I’m convinced.

148
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Both of them are saying it’s you.

149
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:25,000
That’s two accusations out of five.

150
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,000
Hold on! Wait a second!

151
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:29,000
That doesn’t necessarily make it true!

152
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:32,000
Maybe three out of five of us
are the applicants

153
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:34,000
and those two are the infiltrators!

154
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,000
[Kurapika] Not so.

155
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,000
He is not one of the infiltrators.

156
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,000
Excuse me, but…

157
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,000
I think you mean ‘she’, not ‘he’.

158
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,000
I can vouch for you, too.

159
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:47,000
My point is that
none of us can really trust either of you!

160
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:51,000
How do we know
you’re not working together, huh?

161
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,000
[scoffs]

162
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,000
[short woman] Hmm…

163
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:00,000
[scoffs] Anyway, all we’re doing
is wasting time.

164
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,000
We can stand around here all you like,

165
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,000
but it isn’t going to get us anywhere.

166
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,000
[scoffs]

167
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,000
That’s it, then.

168
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:09,000
I’ll have to settle this myself.

169
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:22,000
“My hand makes a punch

170
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,000
and whatever I hit
will burst in flames

171
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,000
-a bunch.”
-Huh?

172
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,000
[all gasp]

173
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,000
This is my power.

174
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
The Wandering Haiku Poet!

175
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Well, dammit.

176
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
It didn’t burn well.
Guess it was a dud.

177
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,000
Huh?

178
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,000
Huh?

179
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:57,000
That was a haiku, if you couldn’t tell,

180
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,000
the prized literary art of my homeland.

181
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,000
Whatever I compose

182
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,000
becomes real.

183
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,000
[all] Huh?

184
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,000
So, there’s your explanation.

185
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,000
Back to the subject at hand.

186
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,000
[gasps]

187
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,000
“If you’re a liar

188
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:19,000
your painful death will be swift
in trial by fire.”

189
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
In other words…

190
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:24,000
anyone who lies to me will burn in hell.

191
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
[gulps]

192
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,000
My question is…

193
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,000
are you an infiltrator?

194
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,000
No, I’m not.

195
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,000
What about you?

196
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:36,000
[short woman] I am not.

197
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
And as for you?

198
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:41,000
Me neither.

199
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:46,000
And are you an infiltrator?

200
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Yeah. I sure am.

201
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,000
[grunts]

202
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:56,000
[poet] I’ll advise you to think carefully
before you answer.

203
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Are you one of the infiltrators?

204
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,000
Well? I’m waiting for an answer!

205
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:07,000
[intense music plays]

206
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,000
[heavy sigh]

207
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,000
My answer’s "Yes, I am."

208
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
[grunts] That was impressive.

209
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,000
I’ll reward you with some information.

210
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,000
My name is Squala.

211
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:34,000
And while I may not have
an official license,

212
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:39,000
I’m a Hunter whose skills
fall into the Manipulator class. Hmm.

213
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,000
I’ve used those abilities

214
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:45,000
to instruct something
to follow a certain order.

215
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,000
It’s true you managed to unmask me,

216
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:51,000
but that doesn’t mean you’ll be able
to escape this mansion alive.

217
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:54,000
[woman] What’s the ‘something’
and what was the order?

218
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,000
[scoffs]

219
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:58,000
That wouldn’t be much of a test,
if I just told you, now would it?

220
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Imbecile.

221
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:02,000
[scoffs]
I’m not gonna talk even if you torture me.

222
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Huh?

223
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,000
[grunts nervously]

224
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,000
[electricity buzzes]

225
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:13,000
[high-pitched voice echoing] Wow!

226
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,000
This is my Nen ability…

227
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Instant Lover.

228
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,000
I am also a Manipulator.

229
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:28,000
I can kiss absolutely anyone

230
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,000
and make them my slave.

231
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,000
[smitten panting]

232
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:34,000
M-- M-- Mistress!

233
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:38,000
[smitten panting]

234
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:41,000
[woman] Take that, and that, and that,
and that, and that!

235
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,000
[Squala] [ecstatic cry] More!

236
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:47,000
Oh, please! Step on me more!

237
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,000
[woman] Now, answer my question!

238
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:52,000
What did you use Nen on
and what was your command?

239
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Say it! C’mon!

240
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:57,000
If you don’t answer me, I’ll stop!

241
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
[Squala] [cries out]
Don't stop! I’ll talk!

242
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:03,000
Yes! I’m just a lowly dog trainer!

243
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,000
[Kurapika] Such a…

244
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,000
[poet] …fearsome power…

245
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:09,000
[Squala] I’ll tell you everything!

246
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:13,000
I used my Nen on the dogs
that run around this mansion!

247
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,000
For example…

248
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:16,000
the Maltese were told
to nip at a target’s feet

249
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,000
to try and slow them down.

250
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,000
That’s when the Saint Bernard comes in!

251
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:24,000
It’s supposed to use its large body
to smother them!

252
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:27,000
And at the exact same time,
the Dobermans will rush in

253
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:29,000
and finish off the target for good!

254
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:32,000
If the target still escapes,
the bulldogs will--

255
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:34,000
-[cries out in pain]
-[woman] That's enough!

256
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,000
Release the Nen you used on the dogs!

257
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
[Squala] Right away!

258
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:49,000
[growling]

259
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,000
So, the dog trainer

260
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:54,000
has been reduced down to a loyal pet, huh?

261
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,000
Oh, don’t say that.

262
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
The only reason I did it
was to make him talk.

263
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,000
If I wanted a man as a pet,

264
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
I could do a whole lot better than him.

265
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
That reminds me,

266
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
I don’t think I ever caught your name.

267
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Mine is Basho.

268
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:11,000
And as you saw just a few minutes ago,
I’m a Conjurer.

269
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
My name is Baise.

270
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,000
I’m Melody.

271
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,000
It seems like you can hear heartbeats.

272
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,000
What category is that?

273
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Oh, you’ll find out soon enough, I’m sure.

274
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Oh, I see. Playing coy then, are we?

275
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,000
What about you?

276
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Hmm. I’d like to know your name
if you don’t mind.

277
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,000
Would you please tell us?

278
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,000
I will not.

279
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,000
We don’t yet know
if we will be working together.

280
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Yes, he has a point.

281
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:47,000
We cleared the first stage
by escaping the mansion,

282
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:49,000
but the real test has only just begun.

283
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:52,000
You're right, we need to locate
one of the designated items

284
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:55,000
from the list we received,
or we can’t get the job.

285
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:58,000
[Basho] If we’re all after the same gig,

286
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,000
we’re bound to run into each other again.

287
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,000
[tall man]
What’s your opinion of this group?

288
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
[Tocino]
This one in particular looks promising.

289
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,000
At least,

290
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,000
more than him.

291
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:20,000
[scoffs] It will be a while
before I require him,

292
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,000
so just put him away for the time being.

293
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,000
I trust you can handle that, Squala.

294
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,000
Y-- Yes, sir.

295
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,000
[Kurapika] If I find one of the objects
and earn the contract,

296
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:47,000
I will have passage
to the Yorknew City auction.

297
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Yes. I will attend!

298
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:52,000
After all,

299
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:56,000
the Phantom Troupe will undoubtedly
be in attendance as well.

300
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:59,000
The band of thieves
that slaughtered my fellow Kurta.

301
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
When we’re overcome with emotion,

302
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,000
our eyes burn a deep scarlet.

303
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:13,000
They were willing to kill
in order to obtain those eyes,

304
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:17,000
considered one of the world’s
seven most beautiful colors.

305
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,000
I will never forgive that act.

306
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,000
I will track them down…

307
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,000
and I will destroy them!

308
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,000
[bird screeching]

309
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,000
[keyboard keys clacking]

310
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:59,000
[Milluki] Hm. So, this is Greed Island.

311
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:03,000
It’s starting to look like
the memory card Kil found

312
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,000
might actually be the real deal.

313
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:09,000
I figured that you could analyze the data

314
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:11,000
and reverse engineer the game itself,
couldn’t you?

315
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:14,000
You bet I can.

316
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:17,000
I’ll strip down the code
and clear the entire game.

317
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:19,000
I’ll put an end to the legend

318
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:23,000
and win 50 billion Jenny in the process.

319
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,000
Oh, right.

320
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,000
This was a trade.

321
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:30,000
I'm gonna have to tell Kil the URL
for the Hunter-only website.

322
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
If I don’t hold up my end of the bargain,

323
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:44,000
that little brat might start talking
about breaking my precious figures again.

324
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,000
[waves crashing]

325
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,000
[Gon] That’s it. Right over there, Killua!

326
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Yeah. We’re almost there. Yorknew.

327
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:07,000
Can you believe we’re gonna
get to see Kurapika and Leorio again?

328
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
I can hardly wait!

329
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:11,000
You’re kinda jumping the gun.

330
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:14,000
We’ve still got two weeks
before we’re supposed to meet up.

331
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Oh, right.

332
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:18,000
It’s been six months
since we saw them last

333
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,000
and I’m getting excited!

334
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,000
And six months ago,

335
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,000
I never would have dreamed
we’d come to Yorknew City.

336
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,000
Not for this, anyway.

337
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,000
[Leorio] Till next time…

338
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,000
[Kurapika] Yes. That will be…

339
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:35,000
[all] September 1st, in Yorknew City!

340
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:39,000
[Killua] The auction starts
on September 1st,

341
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:41,000
so we need to gather as much info
on Greed Island

342
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:43,000
as possible before then.

343
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,000
Mm-hmm. And if we’re lucky,

344
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,000
we might even find out
some more information about Ging.

345
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,000
Well, he did leave you a memory card,

346
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:52,000
along with that recorded message.

347
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,000
There’s gotta be a connection.

348
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,000
But no matter what,

349
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:58,000
once my brother sends that URL to us,

350
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,000
we can check it out, right?

351
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,000
Mm-hmm.

352
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,000
[chuckles softly]

353
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:06,000
-[bird screeching]
-[gasps]

354
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:14,000
[bird screeching]

355
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,000
This is it, Gon.

356
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:26,000
My brother sent the URL.

357
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,000
Wow, that's awesome! Let’s get started!

358
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,000
Yeah!

359
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:35,000
[narrator] Driven by their various goals,

360
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:39,000
Gon and Killua
prepare for September 1st.

361
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:42,000
With the Yorknew City Auction
mere weeks away,

362
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:44,000
there’s no telling what they’ll discover

363
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:46,000
when it begins.

364
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:49,000
[theme song playing]

365
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,000
[Gon] Coming up:

366
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:59,000
-Gon…
-[Killua] …and Killua’s…

367
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:01,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

368
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:02,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

369
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

370
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Today, we're introducing Melody!

371
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,000
She's a Music Hunter!

372
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:09,000
She reads your state of mind
by your heartbeat.

373
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:11,000
So, her senses must be amazing!

374
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:13,000
Hey, Killua, you ate my chocolate?

375
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:14,000
-Nah.
-Not convinced.

376
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:21,000
[Gon] Next time:
"Gathering x Of x Heroes"!

377
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:23,000
Killua! Did you know
I could tell fortunes?

378
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:24,000
[Killua] Really?

379
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
[Gon] Everybody who watched
Hunter x Hunter today is really happy!
